  "description": "I have been informed that we only need permission for the signage, and the internal works do not require listed building consent, as the internal works do not come into contact with any of the historic fabric of the building. But I've included details of the internal works for the sake of clarity.\n\nWe would like to add a golf simulator studio to this part of the building. This space is already a class E space, the space is modern in character with no historic features visible. The ceiling is 4.2 metres tall, but the partition walls are only 3 metres tall, they are only fixed to a raised floor. All of the internal works can be classed as temporary - they could be removed without damaging any of the existing building.\n\nThere will be a sign to the side of the main entrance and two projection signs attached to the outside of the building - all signs will be placed where previous signs were placed, covering any previous damage. ",
